      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "64f2436133ee6009767ab7e9",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I can reproduce this by:\n\n1. Start the Android version of VRChat on a smartphone device\n\n2. Join a world\n\n3. Start the PC version VRChat on a desktop computer\n\n4. Join the same world your smartphone device's client is in\n\n5. The smartphone device's client is disconnected because there are multiple of the same user in the instance, as expected\n\n6. The desktop computer's client will now show the \"Android\" tag on the nameplate, unexpected\n\nTesting shows:\n\n- You can see this yourself, unexpected\n\n- Others can see this, unexpected\n\n- This will persist through instance changes, unexpected\n\n- This will persist until the desktop computer's client is restarted, unexpected\n\nIt is rather funny to join PC only worlds while I have an \"Android\" tag on my nameplate. It can probably really confuse people.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
